hadiths[35]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17303","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said, he said haddathana Thawr, meaning Ibn Yazid, he said haddathani Habib ibn Ubayd, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib Abi Karimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you loves his brother, let him inform him that he loves him."
"17304","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said, he said haddathana Shubah, haddathani Mansur, from al-Shabi, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib Abi Karimah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The night of the guest is obligatory upon every Muslim, so if he wakes in his courtyard deprived, it is a debt upon him, if he wishes he demands it and if he wishes he leaves it."
"17305","Haddathana Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai, he said haddathana Mansur, from Amir, from Abu Karimah, a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night of the guest is obligatory upon every Muslim, so if he wakes in his courtyard deprived, it is a debt upon him, if he wishes he demands it and if he wishes he leaves it."
"17306","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said akhbarana Hariz, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Awf al-Jurashi, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily I have been given the Book and the like of it with it, verily I have been given the Quran and the like of it with it. Soon a man, reclining full upon his couch, will say: Upon you is the Quran, whatever you find in it of lawful deem lawful, and whatever you find in it of unlawful deem unlawful. Verily the flesh of the domestic donkey is not lawful for you, nor every fanged beast of prey. Verily no lost property from the wealth of one under covenant, unless its owner has no need of it. And whoever lodges with a people, it is upon them to host him, and if they do not host him, they have the right to take the like of their hospitality from them."
"17307","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, from Budayl, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam Abi Karimah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever leaves a dependent, then to Allah and His Messenger, and perhaps he said: then to us. And whoever leaves wealth, then to his heir. And the maternal uncle is heir of one who has no heir, and I am heir of one who has no heir, I inherit from him and pay blood money on his behalf."
"17308","Haddathana Hajjaj, he said haddathana Shubah, then he mentioned it, and he said: From al-Miqdam of Kindah, and he was from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17309","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Measure your food, it will be blessed for you in it."
"17310","Haddathana Hajjaj, he said haddathana Shubah, he said I heard Abu al-Judi narrating from Ibn al-Muhajir, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib Abi Karimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whichever Muslim hosts a people and the guest wakes deprived, then it is a duty upon every Muslim to aid him until he takes the hospitality of his night from their crops and wealth."
"17311","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas, he said haddathana Baqiyyah, he said haddathana Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever you feed yourself is charity for you, and whatever you feed your child is charity for you, and whatever you feed your wife is charity for you, and whatever you feed your servant is charity for you."
"17312","Haddathana Surayj ibn al-Numan, haddathana Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, from Artah ibn al-Mundhir, from some elders of the Jund, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding striking the cheeks of beasts, and he said: Allah, Exalted is He, has made for you sticks and whips."
"17313","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas, haddathana Baqiyyah, haddathana Bahir ibn Sad, haddathana Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None of you has eaten food more beloved to Allah, Exalted is He, than from the work of his hand."
"17314","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa and al-Hakam ibn Nafi, they said haddathana Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the martyr with Allah, Exalted is He, al-Hakam said: are six qualities: that he is forgiven at the first shedding of his blood, and he sees, al-Hakam said: and he is shown his seat in Paradise, and he is adorned with the adornment of faith, and he is married from the wide-eyed maidens, and he is protected from the punishment of the grave, and he is safe from the greatest terror, al-Hakam said: the day of the greatest terror, and there is placed upon his head the crown of dignity, a ruby thereof better than the world and what is in it, and he is married to seventy-two wives from the wide-eyed maidens, and he intercedes for seventy persons from his relatives."
"17315","Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Nafi, haddathana Ibn Ayyash, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"17316","Haddathana Haywah ibn Shurayh, haddathana Baqiyyah, haddathana Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, Exalted is He, enjoins you with the nearest then the nearest."
"17317","Haddathana Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, they said haddathana Baqiyyah, haddathana Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade silk and gold and leopard-skin saddle cloths."
"17318","Haddathana Abu al-Mughirah, he said haddathana Sulayman ibn Sulaym al-Kinani, he said haddathana Yahya ibn Jabir al-Tai, he said I heard al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, he said I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The son of Adam has not filled a vessel worse than a belly. Sufficient for the son of Adam are morsels to keep his back straight, and if it must be, then a third for food and a third for drink and a third for his breath."
"17319","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid, he said haddathana Ibn Ayyash, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah, Exalted is He, enjoins you with your mothers, Allah enjoins you with your fathers, Allah enjoins you with the nearest then the nearest."
"17320","Haddathana Abu al-Mughirah, he said haddathana Hariz, he said haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah al-Hadrami, he said I heard al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought ablution water, so he performed ablution, he washed his hands three times, then he washed his face three times, then he washed his forearms three times each, then he rinsed his mouth and nose three times, and wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner, and washed his feet three times each."
"17321","Haddathana Haywah ibn Shurayh, haddathana Baqiyyah, haddathana Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, he said: Al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib and Amr ibn al-Aswad came as a delegation to Muawiyah, so Muawiyah said to al-Miqdam: Did you know that al-Hasan ibn Ali has died. So al-Miqdam said: Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. Muawiyah said to him: Do you consider it a calamity. He said: Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed him in his lap and said: This is from me, and Husayn is from Ali."
"17322","Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Nafi, he said haddathana Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spreading his hands, saying: None of you has eaten food in the world better for him than to eat from the work of his hand."
"17323","Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Nafi, he said haddathana Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whatever you feed yourself is charity for you, and your child, and your wife, and your servant."
"17324","Haddathana Attab, haddathana Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, he said haddathana Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, he said haddathana Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Upon you is the predawn meal, for it is the blessed nourishment."
"17325","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, haddathana Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Kindi, he said I heard al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys and every fanged beast of prey."
"17326","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman and Zayd ibn Hubab, they said haddathana Muawiyah ibn Salih, from al-Hasan ibn Jabir, Zayd said in his hadith: Haddathani al-Hasan ibn Jabir, he said I heard al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade things on the day of Khaybar, then he said: Soon one of you will belie me while reclining upon his couch, narrated my hadith, saying: Between us and you is the Book of Allah, whatever we find in it of lawful we deem lawful, and whatever we find in it of unlawful we deem unlawful. Verily what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade is like what Allah forbade."
"17327","Haddathana Waki and Abu Nuaym, they said haddathana Sufyan, from Mansur, from al-Shabi, from al-Miqdam Abi Karimah, Abu Nuaym said: Al-Miqdam Abu Karimah al-Shami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night of the guest, Abu Nuaym said: is a right, obligatory, so if he wakes in his courtyard, it is a debt upon him, if he wishes he demands and if he wishes he leaves."
"17328","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, he said I heard Mansur narrating from al-Shabi, from al-Miqdam Abi Karimah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Upon every Muslim the night of the guest is an obligatory right, so if he wakes in his courtyard, it is a debt upon him, if he wishes he demands and if he wishes he leaves."
"17329","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah, he said I heard Abu al-Judi narrating from Said ibn al-Muhajir, from al-Miqdam Abi Karimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whichever Muslim hosts a people and the guest wakes deprived, then it is a right upon every Muslim to aid him until he takes the hospitality of the night, his night, from their crops and wealth."
"17330","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said haddathana Shubah, he said Abu al-Judi informed me that he heard Said ibn al-Muhajir, that he heard al-Miqdam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says, then he mentioned the like of it."
"17331","Haddathana Hammad ibn Khalid, he said haddathana Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Rashid ibn Sad, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever leaves wealth, then to his heirs, and whoever leaves debt or dependents, then to me, and I am the guardian of one who has no guardian, I release his burden and inherit his wealth, and the maternal uncle is guardian of one who has no guardian, he releases his burden and inherits his wealth."
"17332","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said I heard Rashid ibn Sad narrating from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned the like of it, except he said: I release his burden."
"17333","Haddathana Abu al-Yaman, he said haddathana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, he said: Al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib had a slave girl who sold milk, and al-Miqdam took the price, so it was said to him: Glory be to Allah, do you sell milk and take the price. He said: Yes, and what is wrong with that, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will come upon people a time in which only the dinar and the dirham will avail."
"17334","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan, from Mansur, from al-Shabi, from al-Miqdam Abi Karimah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night of the guest is obligatory, so if he wakes in his courtyard, it is a debt for him, if he wishes he demands and if he wishes he leaves."
"17335","Haddathana Abu Kamil, haddathana Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, he said haddathana Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves debt or dependents, then to me, and whoever leaves wealth, then to his heir, and I am the patron of one who has no patron, I inherit his wealth and release his captive, and the maternal uncle is patron of one who has no patron, he inherits his wealth and releases his captive."
"17336","Haddathana Affan, he said haddathana Shubah, he said Budayl al-Uqayli informed me, he said I heard Ali ibn Abi Talhah narrating from Rashid ibn Sad, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam, from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever leaves a dependent, then to me, he said, and perhaps he said: to Allah and to His Messenger. And whoever leaves wealth, then to his heirs. And I am heir of one who has no heir, I pay blood money on his behalf and inherit from him, and the maternal uncle is heir of one who has no heir, he pays blood money on his behalf and inherits from him."
"17337","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Harrani, haddathana Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash, haddathana Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam, from his grandfather al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have succeeded, O Qudaym, if you are not a commander, nor a collector, nor a headman."
